@startuml state_workout_session
title FitTrack — State Machine Diagram: WorkoutSession
hide empty description

[*] --> NotStarted : new WorkoutSession(body_kg)

NotStarted --> InProgress : start() / start timer
NotStarted --> Cancelled : cancel()

InProgress : entry / timer running
InProgress : log_set(ex, reps, kg) / validate, add set, recalc
InProgress : log_cardio(ex, min) / validate, add minutes, recalc
InProgress : exit / bank elapsed time

Paused : entry / timer stopped
Paused : log_set / reject (InvalidTransition)

InProgress --> Paused : pause()
Paused --> InProgress : resume() / restart timer

InProgress --> Completed : finish() [has logged work] / build summary, save
Paused --> Completed : finish() [has logged work] / build summary, save
InProgress --> InProgress : finish() [no logged work] / show error

InProgress --> Cancelled : cancel() [user confirms]
Paused --> Cancelled : cancel() [user confirms]

Completed --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]

note right of Completed
  Terminal states: every further event
  raises InvalidTransition.
  Verified by tests/test_session_state.py
  (all 5 states x 5 events = 25 pairs).
end note
@enduml
